          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em JT-gravity
            (
            %a{:href => "#Teitelboim83"}> Teitelboim 83
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Jackiw85"} Jackiw 85
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+gravity"} in 1+1 dimensions
            with a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dilaton"} dilaton
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToNearExtremalBlackHoles Relation to near-extremal black holes
          %p
            JT-gravity gives a good approximation to the
            = succeed "-factor" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} AdS
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near+horizon+geometry"} near horizon geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi AdS
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_2\times S^{d-2}
            of near-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremal+black+holes"} extremal black holes
            in
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#NSST18"} NSST18
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#MTV18"} MTV18
          %p
            Via the
            = succeed "-dual" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT"} AdS/CFT
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#AlmheiriPolchinski14"} Almheiri-Polchinski 14
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/random+matrix+theory"} random matrix theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#SaadShenkerStanford19"}> Saad-Shenker-Stanford 19
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#StanfordWitten19"} Stanford-Witten 19
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SYK+model"} SYK model
            = succeed "-aspects" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremal+black+holes"} extremal black holes
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole+entropy"} black hole entropy
          %p
            Notice that near-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremal+black+holes"} extremal black holes
            have been observed in nature, by the Chandra telescope
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://scitechdaily.com/chandra-views-spinning-black-holes-across-cosmic-sea/"} see eg here
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SYK+model"} SYK model
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Liouville+theory"} Liouville theory
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The theory is due to
          %ul
            %li#Teitelboim83
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Teitelboim"}> Claudio Teitelboim
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gravitation and hamiltonian structure in two spacetime dimensions
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(83)90012-6"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(83)90012-6
            %li#Jackiw85
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roman+Jackiw"}> Roman Jackiw
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lower dimensional gravity
              %p
                Volume 252, 1985, Pages 343-356 (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(85)90448-1"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(85)90448-1
                )
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              Gustavo J. Turiaci:
              %em Les Houches lectures on two-dimensional gravity and holography
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.09537"}> arXiv:2412.09537
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jackiw%E2%80%93Teitelboim_gravity"} Jackiw-Teitelboim gravity
          %p Further development:
          %ul
            %li
